(18: (meta: (t: semantic) (n: 1) (term: string%20value) (def: %23%20Vision%20%26%20implementation%3A%20a%20universal%2C%20self-describing%20meta%20language%20with%20a%20links-network%20CST%2FAST%20for%20any%20language%0A%0A%3E%20%2A%2ATerminology%20note%20for%20this%20repository%3A%2A%2A%20we%20use%20%2A%2Alinks%20network%2A%2A%20everywhere%2C%20and%20we%20model%20everything%20as%20%2A%2Alinks%2A%2A%20in%20the%20sense%20of%20Links%20Theory%20%28%5Blink-foundation%2Fmeta-theory%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-foundation%2Fmeta-theory%29%29.%20The%20word%20%2A%2Agraph%2A%2A%20is%20%2A%2Aforbidden%2A%2A%20in%20this%20repository%20%E2%80%94%20not%20as%20a%20stylistic%20preference%20but%20as%20a%20design%20commitment%2C%20because%20Links%20Theory%20deliberately%20%2A%2Aeliminates%20the%20node%2Fedge%20dichotomy%2A%2A%20that%20graph%20theory%20is%20built%20on.%20Per%20the%20foundational%20article%3A%20%2A%22a%20link%20is%20defined%20as%20an%20n-tuple%20of%20references%20to%20links%22%2A%3B%20%2A%22a%20vertex%20is%20equivalent%20to%20a%20self-referential%20link%20%E2%80%94%20a%20link%20that%20begins%20and%20ends%20in%20itself%22%2A%3B%20%2A%22a%20directed%20edge%20is%20represented%20as%20a%20directed%20doublet-link%22%2A%3B%20and%20%2A%22while%20graph%20theory%20requires%20two%20types%20of%20entities%20%E2%80%94%20vertices%20and%20edges%20%E2%80%94%20in%20the%20links%20theory%20only%20links%20%28which%20most%20closely%20resemble%20edges%29%20are%20necessary.%22%2A%0A%3E%0A%3E%20So%20in%20this%20repository%20%2A%2Aboth%20a%20%22node%22%20and%20an%20%22edge%22%20are%20links%2A%2A%3A%20a%20node%20is%20just%20a%20self-referential%20link%20%28e.g.%20%60%28x%3A%20x%20x%29%60%29%2C%20and%20what%20would%20be%20an%20edge%20is%20an%20ordinary%20link%20connecting%20other%20links.%20We%20never%20treat%20node%20and%20edge%20as%20two%20kinds%20of%20primitive.%20A%20%2A%2Areference%2A%2A%20is%20a%20link%27s%20pointer%20to%20another%20link.%20When%20an%20external%20dependency%20%28tree-sitter%2C%20etc.%29%20speaks%20of%20nodes%2Fedges%2Fgraphs%2C%20we%20translate%20to%20links%2Flinks-network%20at%20the%20boundary.%20This%20mirrors%20the%20convention%20already%20established%20in%20%5Blink-assistant%2Fmeta-expression%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-assistant%2Fmeta-expression%29%20and%20%5Blink-assistant%2Fformal-ai%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-assistant%2Fformal-ai%29.%0A%0A%23%23%200.%20One-line%20vision%0A%0AA%20%2A%2Ameta%20language%2A%2A%3A%20a%20single%20mutable%2C%20self-describing%20%2A%2Alinks%20network%2A%2A%20that%20can%20losslessly%20represent%20the%20CST%2C%20AST%2C%20and%20semantic%20structure%20of%20%2A%2Aany%2A%2A%20programming%20or%20natural%20language%20%E2%80%94%20and%20that%20%2A%2Adescribes%20itself%20fully%20in%20its%20own%20terms%2A%2A%2C%20including%20the%20common%20roots%20of%20the%20common%20ontologies%2C%20with%20clear%20definitions%20of%20every%20term%20written%20in%20those%20terms%20themselves.%0A%0AIt%20is%20the%20structural%20substrate%20that%20%5Blink-assistant%2Fformal-ai%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-assistant%2Fformal-ai%29%20and%20%5Blink-assistant%2Fmeta-expression%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-assistant%2Fmeta-expression%29%20need%20underneath%20their%20formalization%20%2F%20deformalization%20work%3A%20a%20place%20to%20%2A%2Aparse%20raw%20text%20into%20a%20CST%2FAST%2Fnetwork%20for%20a%20selected%20language%2C%20verify%20whether%20the%20text%20fully%20matches%20that%20language%2C%20parse%20a%20mix%20of%20languages%20with%20auto-detected%20regions%2C%20transform%20the%20network%20by%20substitution%20rules%2C%20and%20reconstruct%20it%20back%20to%20a%20%28possibly%20different%29%20target%20language.%2A%2A%0A%0A%23%23%201.%20Why%20this%20exists%20%E2%80%94%20the%20gap%0A%0AExisting%20lossless-CST%20tooling%20is%20excellent%20but%20%2A%2Aper-ecosystem%20and%20tree-shaped%2A%2A%3A%0A%0A-%20%2A%2Atree-sitter%2A%2A%20parses%20essentially%20any%20language%20into%20a%20concrete%20syntax%20tree%2C%20but%3A%20it%20keeps%20%2A%2AN%20disjoint%2C%20range-keyed%20trees%2A%2A%20for%20mixed-language%20documents%20%28the%20host%20app%20must%20correlate%20them%29%2C%20its%20trivia%20%2Afloats%2A%20as%20%60extra%60%20sibling%20links%20rather%20than%20being%20attached%2C%20its%20injection%2Fauto-detection%20is%20%2A%2Aname-driven%2C%20not%20content-driven%2A%2A%2C%20and%20it%20does%20not%20pretty-print%20or%20guarantee%20transform-and-reconstruct%20round-trips.%0A-%20%2A%2ALibCST%2A%2A%20%28Python%29%2C%20%2A%2ARecast%2A%2A%2F%2A%2Ajscodeshift%2A%2A%20%28JS%2FTS%29%2C%20%2A%2ARowan%2A%2A%2F%2A%2Acstree%2A%2A%20%28Rust%29%2C%20%2A%2ARoslyn%2A%2A%20%28C%23%29%20each%20give%20a%20great%20lossless%20parse%E2%86%92transform%E2%86%92reprint%20pipeline%20%E2%80%94%20but%20only%20for%20their%20%2A%2Aone%2A%2A%20language%2C%20and%20only%20%2A%2Asame-language%2A%2A%20round-tripping.%20None%20of%20them%20targets%20%2Across-language%2A%20reconstruction.%0A-%20None%20of%20them%20is%20%2A%2Aself-describing%2A%2A%2C%20and%20all%20of%20them%20are%20trees%20%28single-parent%20containment%29%20that%20reach%20for%20ad-hoc%20side%20tables%20when%20they%20need%20cross-references%2C%20data%20flow%2C%20or%20shared%2Fcyclic%20structure.%20In%20a%20links%20network%20there%20is%20no%20such%20impedance%3A%20cross-references%2C%20flow%2C%20and%20sharing%20are%20just%20more%20links%2C%20because%20there%20is%20no%20privileged%20node%2Fedge%20distinction%20to%20work%20around.%0A%0AThe%20interesting%20requirement%20%E2%80%94%20%2Aparse%20language%20A%2C%20transform%2C%20reconstruct%20as%20language%20B%2A%20%E2%80%94%20and%20the%20requirement%20to%20reason%20%2A%2Aby%20meaning%2A%2A%20%28not%20just%20syntax%29%20both%20demand%20a%20representation%20richer%20than%20a%20tree.%20A%20links%20network%20is%20that%20representation%2C%20and%20it%20is%20the%20one%20our%20ecosystem%20is%20already%20built%20on.%0A%0A%23%23%202.%20Foundations%20we%20build%20on%20%28and%20must%20stay%20compatible%20with%29%0A%0AThis%20project%20sits%20on%20top%20of%2C%20and%20must%20remain%20compatible%20with%2C%20the%20existing%20link-foundation%20%2F%20link-assistant%20stack%3A%0A%0A%7C%20Project%20%7C%20What%20it%20gives%20us%20%7C%20How%20we%20use%20it%20%7C%0A%7C---%7C---%7C---%7C%0A%7C%20%5Blink-foundation%2Fmeta-theory%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-foundation%2Fmeta-theory%29%20%7C%20The%20Links%20Theory%20%2F%20Deep%20Theory%20articles%20%E2%80%94%20the%20conceptual%20root.%20Defines%20a%20link%20as%20%2A%22an%20n-tuple%20of%20references%20to%20links%22%2A%20and%20unifies%20vertices%2Fedges%20into%20links%20%7C%20Our%20ontology%20roots%20and%20the%20definitions%20of%20%22link%22%20%2F%20%22reference%22%20trace%20back%20here%3B%20the%20node%2Fedge-as-links%20unification%20is%20foundational%20to%20our%20whole%20model%20%7C%0A%7C%20%5Blink-foundation%2Flinks-notation%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-foundation%2Flinks-notation%29%20%28%2A%2Anote%3A%20%60links-notation%60%2C%20plural%20%E2%80%94%20%60link-notation%60%20404s%2A%2A%29%20%7C%20%2A%2ALiNo%2A%2A%20%E2%80%94%20the%20textual%20surface%3A%20doublets%20%60%28lovesMama%3A%20loves%20mama%29%60%2C%20triplets%20%60papa%20has%20car%60%2C%20N-tuples%2C%20indented%20syntax.%20%2A%22structured%20data%20as%20links%20between%20references%20to%20links%22%2A%20%7C%20The%20human-readable%20serialization%20of%20our%20network%3B%20%60%28index%3A%20source%20target%20...%29%60%20is%20our%20link%20form%2C%20and%20a%20self-referential%20link%20is%20our%20%22point%22%20%7C%0A%7C%20%5Blink-foundation%2Flink-cli%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-foundation%2Flink-cli%29%20%7C%20The%20%2A%2Asingle%20Turing-complete%20operation%2A%2A%3A%20match-pattern%20%E2%86%92%20substitute-pattern%2C%20with%20%60%24index%2F%24source%2F%24target%60%20variables%3B%20CRUD%20all%20expressed%20via%20one%20substitution%20%7C%20Our%20transformation%20engine.%20Every%20transform%20%28formalize%2C%20deformalize%2C%20rename%2C%20inline%2C%20cross-language%20map%29%20is%20substitution%20over%20the%20network%20%7C%0A%7C%20%5Blink-foundation%2Flino-objects-codec%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-foundation%2Flino-objects-codec%29%20%7C%20Encoding%20arbitrary%20objects%20to%2Ffrom%20LiNo%20with%20%2A%2Atyped%20links%2A%2A%2C%20%2A%2Aidentity%20%26%20circular-reference%20preservation%2A%2A%20%7C%20How%20we%20serialize%20the%20mutable%20network%20and%20its%20snapshots%3B%20circular%2Fshared%20structure%20is%20native%2C%20not%20a%20special%20case%20%7C%0A%7C%20%5Blink-foundation%2Frelative-meta-logic%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-foundation%2Frelative-meta-logic%29%20%7C%20%22Everything%20is%20a%20link%22%20%2B%20dependent%20types%20%60%28Type%3A%20Type%20Type%29%60%2C%20many-valued%2Fprobabilistic%20evaluation%2C%20export%20to%20Lean%2FCoq%2FIsabelle%20%7C%20The%20semantic%2Ftyping%20layer%3B%20matching%20%22by%20meaning%22%20and%20verifying%20%22text%20fully%20matches%20a%20language%22%20can%20lean%20on%20RML-style%20evaluation%20%7C%0A%7C%20%5Blink-assistant%2Fformal-ai%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-assistant%2Fformal-ai%29%20%7C%20Consumer%3A%20%22Links%20Notation%20as%20the%20universal%20intermediate%20representation%22%2C%20%22one%20doublet-links%20store%20is%20the%20source%20of%20truth%22%2C%20%22parses%20languages%20into%20a%20links%20network%20%28not%20graph%29%22%20%7C%20We%20provide%20the%20structural%20network%20it%20formalizes%20into%3B%20we%20can%20replay%20its%20%2A%2A706-case%20corpus%2A%2A%20as%20a%20parity%20gate%20%7C%0A%7C%20%5Blink-assistant%2Fmeta-expression%5D%28https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Flink-assistant%2Fmeta-expression%29%20%7C%20The%20most%20mature%20%2A%2Aformalize%20%E2%86%94%20deformalize%20%2F%20naturalize%2A%2A%20round-trip%3B%20CST%20with%20phrase%20ids%2C%20token%2Fsource%20spans%2C%20entity%20ids%3B%20the%20%60semantic-lexicon.json%60%20interlingua%20%28328%20concepts%2C%20en%2Fhi%2Fru%2Fzh%29%20%7C%20Defines%20the%20formalization%2Fdeformalization%20contract%20we%20must%20support%20and%20configure%20%7C%0A%0A%2A%2AThe%20single%20Turing-complete%20operation%20from%20%60link-cli%60%20is%20the%20heart%20of%20our%20transform%20layer.%2A%2A%20We%20do%20not%20invent%20a%20new%20transformation%20calculus%3B%20we%20adopt%20match-and-substitute%20over%20links%20and%20make%20the%20%2Amatcher%2A%20richer%20%28by%20syntax%2C%20by%20meaning%2C%20by%20type%29.%0A%0A%23%23%203.%20What%20we%20must%20support%20%28requirements%29%0A%0A%23%23%23%203.1%20Universal%20structural%20representation%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20A%20mutable%20links%20network%20that%20can%20represent%20%2A%2ACST%2A%2A%20%28every%20token%2C%20every%20comma%2Fparen%2C%20all%20trivia%29%2C%20%2A%2AAST%2A%2A%20%28named%2Fabstract%20structure%29%2C%20and%20%2A%2Asemantic%2A%2A%20relations%20%28use%E2%86%92def%2C%20call%E2%86%92body%2C%20data%20flow%2C%20coreference%2C%20types%29%20%2A%2Asimultaneously%20over%20the%20same%20links%2A%2A%20%E2%80%94%20because%20these%20are%20different%20link-sets%2C%20not%20different%20trees.%20%28There%20is%20no%20separate%20%22node%20table%22%20and%20%22edge%20table%22%3A%20all%20of%20it%20is%20one%20set%20of%20links.%29%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20%2A%2ALossless%2A%2A%20by%20construction%3A%20the%20network%20retains%20enough%20to%20reprint%20the%20exact%20original%20source%2C%20byte-for-byte%20%28the%20LibCST%2FRoslyn%2FRowan%20guarantee%29%2C%20with%20trivia%20attached%20via%20explicit%20links%20%28our%20divergence%20from%20tree-sitter%27s%20floating%20%60extra%60%20links%20%E2%80%94%20we%20should%20support%20both%20%2Acontainment-link-attached%2A%20%28Rowan-style%29%20and%20%2Atoken-link-attached%2A%20%28Roslyn-style%29%20trivia%20as%20a%20configurable%20policy%29.%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20Rich%20per-link%20metadata%20matching%20what%20tree-sitter%20projects%20expect%3A%20link%20type%2C%20%2A%2Anamed%20vs%20anonymous%2A%2A%2C%20%2A%2Afields%20as%20labeled%20links%2A%2A%2C%20byte%20ranges%2C%20row%2Fcolumn%20points%2C%20and%20flags%20%60isError%60%20%2F%20%60hasError%60%20%2F%20%60isMissing%60%20%2F%20%60isExtra%60.%20%28tree-sitter%27s%20%22fields%22%20%E2%80%94%20a%20labeled%20parent%E2%86%92child%20relation%20%E2%80%94%20are%20themselves%20just%20links%20here%2C%20not%20a%20separate%20concept%20layered%20on%20positional%20children.%29%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20%2A%2AError%20recovery%20%2F%20partial%20parsing%2A%2A%3A%20always%20produce%20a%20network%20even%20on%20invalid%20input%20%28ERROR%2FMISSING%20modeled%20as%20links%29%2C%20so%20we%20can%20answer%20%22does%20this%20text%20%2Afully%2A%20match%20language%20X%3F%22%20precisely%20%28clean%20%E2%87%94%20no%20error%2Fmissing%20links%20in%20the%20region%29.%0A%0A%23%23%23%203.2%20Parse%20%2F%20verify%20%2F%20mixed%20languages%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20%60parse%28text%2C%20language%29%20-%3E%20network%60%20for%20a%20%2A%2Aselected%2A%2A%20language%20%28programming%20or%20natural%29.%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20%2A%2AVerify%2A%2A%20a%20text%20fully%20matches%20a%20language%20%28full-match%20check%2C%20returning%20the%20failing%20regions%2Flinks%20if%20not%29.%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20%2A%2AMixed-language%20parsing%20with%20auto-detected%20regions%2A%2A%20%E2%80%94%20e.g.%20documentation%20containing%20prose%20plus%20fenced%20code%20blocks%20parsed%20as%20one%20network.%20Unlike%20tree-sitter%2C%20the%20result%20is%20%2A%2Aone%20unified%20network%2A%2A%20with%20cross-language%20links%20keyed%20on%20shared%20byte%20ranges%2C%20not%20N%20disjoint%20trees.%20Support%20both%20%2A%2Aname-driven%2A%2A%20detection%20%28fenced%20%60%20%60%60%60rust%20%60%29%20%2Aand%2A%20%2A%2Acontent-driven%2A%2A%20auto-detection%20%28sniffing%29%20as%20our%20explicit%20addition.%0A%0A%23%23%23%203.3%20Self-description%20%28the%20%22meta%22%20in%20meta-language%29%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20The%20meta%20language%20%2A%2Adescribes%20itself%20fully%20in%20its%20own%20terms%2A%2A%3A%20the%20definitions%20of%20%60link%60%2C%20%60reference%60%2C%20%60relation%20link%60%2C%20%60language%60%2C%20%60grammar%60%2C%20%60type%60%2C%20%60concept%60%20%28and%20the%20fact%20that%20a%20%22node%22%20is%20just%20a%20self-referential%20link%20and%20an%20%22edge%22%20just%20a%20connecting%20link%29%20are%20all%20themselves%20links%20in%20the%20network%2C%20with%20%2A%2Aclear%20definitions%20written%20in%20those%20very%20terms%2A%2A.%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20Include%20the%20%2A%2Acommon%20roots%20of%20the%20common%20ontologies%2A%2A%20%E2%80%94%20one%20shared%20set%20of%20base%20concepts%2Ftypes%2Fterms%20from%20which%20language-specific%20vocabularies%20derive.%20%28Ties%20into%20relative-meta-logic%27s%20%60%28Type%3A%20Type%20Type%29%60%20self-referential%20root%20and%20meta-expression%27s%20controlled%20R-terminology.%29%0A%0A%23%23%23%203.4%20Shared%20concepts%20mapped%20to%20per-language%20syntax%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20A%20%2A%2Acommon%20concept%20layer%2A%2A%3A%20e.g.%20a%20shared%20set%20of%20concepts%20for%20%2A%2Afunctional%2A%2A%20and%20%2A%2Aprocedural%2A%2A%20languages%20%28function%2C%20binding%2C%20application%2C%20sequence%2C%20branch%2C%20loop%2C%20...%29%2C%20each%20mapped%20to%20%2A%2Adifferent%20concrete%20syntax%2A%2A%20in%20different%20specific%20languages%20%E2%80%94%20and%20languages%20that%20%2A%2Amix%2A%2A%20these%20features%20%28most%20real%20languages%29%20compose%20the%20concept%20sets.%20Two%20languages%20sharing%20a%20concept%20must%20reference%20the%20%2A%2Asame%2A%2A%20concept%20link%2C%20not%20duplicate%20it.%20This%20is%20what%20makes%20cross-language%20transformation%20meaningful.%0A%0A%23%23%23%203.5%20Snapshots%20%26%20mutation%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20%2A%2AImmutable%20snapshots%2A%2A%20%28persistent%2C%20structurally%20shared%20%E2%80%94%20the%20property%20that%20makes%20tree-sitter%27s%20per-keystroke%20reparse%20and%20thread-sharing%20cheap%29%20%2A%2Aand%2A%2A%20%2A%2Amutable%20snapshots%2A%2A%20for%20in-place%20editing.%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20Versioning%20of%20the%20network%20over%20time%20%28link-cli%20already%20models%20named%20references%2C%20triggers%2C%20and%20persistent%20transformation%3B%20meta-expression%20already%20stores%20%60version%60%2F%60provenance%60%29.%0A%0A%23%23%23%203.6%20Transformation%20by%20substitution%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20Apply%20transformations%20via%20%2A%2Asubstitution%20rules%2A%2A%20built%20on%20link-cli%27s%20single%20operation%3A%20match-pattern%20%E2%86%92%20substitute-pattern.%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20%2A%2AAdvanced%20matching%2A%2A%3A%20by%20%2A%2Asyntax%2A%2A%20%28structural%20pattern%2C%20tree-sitter-query-like%20S-expressions%20over%20links%20%E2%80%94%20quantifiers%2C%20alternation%2C%20anchors%2C%20captures%2C%20fields%2C%20negated%20fields%29%2C%20by%20%2A%2Ameaning%2A%2A%20%28semantic%2Fconcept-level%20match%20via%20the%20common%20concept%20layer%20%2B%20relative-meta-logic%20evaluation%29%2C%20and%20by%20%2A%2Atype%2A%2A.%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20Predicates%2Ftext%20conditions%20stay%20a%20%2A%2Apluggable%20host-evaluated%20layer%2A%2A%2C%20mirroring%20tree-sitter%27s%20split%20%28engine%20does%20structural%20matching%20%2B%20capture%20binding%3B%20host%20does%20regex%2Feq%2Fsemantic%20predicates%29.%0A%0A%23%23%23%203.7%20Reconstruction%20%26%20cross-language%20target%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20%2A%2AReconstruct%2A%2A%20the%20network%20back%20to%20text%20%E2%80%94%20same%20language%20%28lossless%20round-trip%20for%20unchanged%20regions%2C%20clean%20pretty-print%20for%20changed%20regions%29%20%2A%2Aand%2A%2A%20to%20a%20%2A%2Adifferent%20target%20language%2A%2A%20via%20the%20common%20concept%20layer%20%28concept%20%E2%86%92%20target%20syntax%29.%0A-%20%5B%20%5D%20%2A%2AConfigurable%20formalization%20%2F%20deformalization%20%28naturalization%29%2A%2A%20%E2%80%94%20the%20way%20we%20go%20text%20%E2%86%92%20network%20and%20network%20%E2%86%92%20text%20must%20be%20configurable%2C%20since%20that%20is%20exactly%20the%20knob%20formal-ai%20and%20meta-expression%20need%20%28%60translateTextWith%28%29%60%20%2F%20%60naturalize%60%20%2F%20%60deformalize%60%20semantics%2C%20formalization%20levels%201%E2%80%934%20with%20executable%20gating%29.%0A%0A%23%23%204.%20Architectur